@startuml "Vérification d'email - Diagramme de séquence"

title Processus de vérification d'email

actor "Utilisateur" as User
participant "Frontend\n(Next.js)" as Frontend
participant "API Gateway\n(Rate Limiter)" as API
participant "Auth Controller" as AuthCtrl
participant "User Service" as UserSvc
participant "Redis Cache" as Redis
participant "Database\n(PostgreSQL)" as DB

== Vérification email ==
User -> User: Cliquer lien email
activate User
User -> Frontend: GET /verify-email?token=xyz
activate Frontend

Frontend -> API: POST /api/auth/verify-email
note right: Body: {token}
activate API

API -> AuthCtrl: verifyEmail(token)
activate AuthCtrl

AuthCtrl -> Redis: GET verify:{token}
activate Redis
Redis --> AuthCtrl: userId
deactivate Redis

alt Token valide et non expiré
    AuthCtrl -> UserSvc: updateUser(userId, {isVerified: true})
    activate UserSvc
    UserSvc -> DB: UPDATE users SET isVerified=true WHERE id=?
    activate DB
    DB --> UserSvc: user updated
    deactivate DB
    deactivate UserSvc
    
    AuthCtrl -> Redis: DEL verify:{token}
    activate Redis
    Redis --> AuthCtrl: token deleted
    deactivate Redis
    
    AuthCtrl --> API: email verified
    deactivate AuthCtrl
    API --> Frontend: verification success
    deactivate API
    Frontend --> User: "Email vérifié, vous pouvez vous connecter"
    deactivate Frontend
    
else Token invalide ou expiré
    AuthCtrl --> API: 400 Bad Request "Invalid or expired token"
    deactivate AuthCtrl
    API --> Frontend: verification failed
    deactivate API
    Frontend --> User: "Lien invalide ou expiré"
    deactivate Frontend
end

deactivate User

note over User, DB
    Une fois l'email vérifié, l'utilisateur 
    peut se connecter à l'application
end note

@enduml